-- `boundary.md` §9.4.5's runtime checks, check 4: each export of a markup
-- runtime takes the parameters its caller passes. The platform `views`
-- names `ssr` with a runtime of its own whose `list` takes two where the
-- lowering declares three — reported in the runtime, at the export — and
-- whose `map` takes one where `html`'s primitive takes two — reported at
-- the primitive's declaration, naming the runtime's line. Nothing is
-- written.
import Node exposing (Program)


main : Program
main =
    Node.print "hello"
